sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 3, docs/reference/development-containers.md#the-default-instance): the Project's first default Instance on an app-dev Node, the only Instance built from scratch. It runs no T3; it is the clone source of the Project's other Instances. When the charts move into place, this becomes the first-default branch of container/create.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:create PROJECT NODE default
  %% kind: instance.create
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:create<br/>PROJECT NODE default
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:create PROJECT NODE default`
  %%> - a name equal to the Project's default branch also creates the `default` Instance
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve default<br/>address · .env
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has node access to the target Node, an active `app-dev` Node
  %%> - the Project has no default Instance anywhere in the fleet; its other Instances are made on this Node
  %%> - a web-serving Project names its PHP version, and the runtime folder holds that static PHP build
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the default Instance is reserved with its runtime record and Route; it gets no T3 port
  %%> - `.env` is rendered from the Project's env template; a repository read token goes to the vault
  Note over GW: Commit, push copies<br/>queue start · answer 202
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  GW->>SW: Start run from queue<br/>operation-instance-create
  SW->>N: Launch the container<br/>Ansible · tags container
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `incus init` from the Node's image `orbit-instance` with the reserved bridge address, then `incus start`; the project's profile gives `security.port_isolation` and the idmapped, read-only shared folders
  %%> - the NIC carries `orbitinst0-proxy` and the container's own ACL, which lets only the Node's Caddy reach port 8080; `orbitinst0-egress` stays on the bridge only
  %%> - the agent folder is mounted too, so its clones have it; nothing in the default runs from it
  %%> - fetches the default branch into the Node's mirror with the read token; the token stays on the Node
  %%> Mail:
  %%> - the same launch applies the exact SMTP path before the four root-owned mail units; no separate mail playbook or step
  %%> - two IPv4 loopback sockets forward 1025 and 2525; foreign units or listeners skip setup without stopping their Process
  opt database on a Database server
    SW->>N: Create the database<br/>child operation-database-create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the database family creates the owner and the database on the Project's database server, on this Node or another
    %%> - needs the container's database rule; without it the admission refuses `operation.kind_unavailable`
  end
  SW->>C: Prepare the workspace<br/>Ansible · tags workspace
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - pushes the default branch in as a bundle and checks it out in `/srv/workspace` as `orbit`, with the group, setgid bits and default ACLs
  %%> - writes `.env` for `orbit` with group `work`; writes no `/etc/orbit/instance`, so T3 never starts here
  SW->>C: Run dev deploy steps<br/>incus exec · vault copy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the Project's development deploy steps, as `orbit`, in list order: they install dependencies and migrate
  %%> - the runtime folder supplies `php`, `composer`, Node and Bun; dependency downloads use the container egress model
  SW->>C: Start Processes<br/>Ansible · tags processes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - FrankenPHP starts as the `orbit` unit `orbit-frankenphp.service` on port 8080 of the bridge address
  %%> - writes the shared FrankenPHP Caddyfile: only the Node's bridge peer with `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` sets PHP's HTTPS scheme, port and resolved client IP; other requests keep native values
  %%> - starts use nonblocking systemd jobs, then a bounded readiness check for each running unit; container Process units order after `network.target`
  %%> - the Project's development Processes start as `orbit-process-<id>-<name>.service` units, as `orbit`; each environment file comes from the vault, root only
  %%> - a Process whose desired state is stopped is installed, not started
  opt web-serving Project
    SW->>N: Create the Route<br/>child operation-route-create
  end
  SW->>N: Take the seed snapshot<br/>Ansible · tags seed
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops the Processes for a moment and snapshots the container as `seed-<commit>`, which clones copy
  alt all steps pass in budget
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record default Instance<br/>active · seed commit
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the default Instance is active and its container runs; the runtime records the seed commit
  else a step fails or the budget ends
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    %%> What stays:
    %%> - the stopped container with its workspace, marked failed; the same command resumes it
    Note over GW: Record the failure
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
